        <headline>DUAL BLEED ISSUE - WORK ORDER CANNOT BE PUSHED</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: ACMS DATA SHOWS LH BLEED TRIP IN CLIMB. RH DUCT PRESSURE IS ALSO LOW IN DESCENT. THIS WORK ORDER HAS BEEN RAISED TO TROUBLESHOOT THE LH BLEED ISSUE.

** LH BLEED SYSTEM TROUBLESHOOTING TO BE PRIORITIES **  
 
ACTION:  
 
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #1 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.      

* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM        

** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.

3. INSPECT THE LH BAR HARNESS FOR PATH TO GROUND ON PINS 9 + 10 OF DP1102 OF BLEED AIR REGULATOR - IF CONTINUITY FOUND REFERENCE WDM 36-11-11 BLEED AIR VALVE CONTROL TO ISOLATE S20 OVERTEMP SWITCH. IF NIL FAULT FOUND PROCEED TO STEP 3.
 
4. CHECK FOR CONTINUITY THROUGH LH BLEED AIR REGULATOR 220 PRESSURE SWITCH AT PINS 9 AND 10 OF BLEED AIR REGULATOR M1180 - IF CONTINUITY IS FOUND REPLACE BLEED AIR REGULATOR IAW AMM 36-11-03/401 BLEED AIR REGULATOR - REMOVAL/INSTALLATION.
 
5. IF TROUBLESHOOTING IS INDETERMINATE DUE TO THE INTERMITTENT NATURE:

REPLACE THE LH BAR HARNESS (MW0311) IAW AMM 73-21-06/401.
 
REPLACE LH ACAU IAW AMM 21-51-02/401 AIR CONDITIONING ACCESSORY UNIT (ACAU) - REMOVAL/INSTALLATION.
 
REPLACE LH BLEED AIR REGULATOR IAW AMM 36-11-03/401 BLEED AIR REGULATOR - REMOVAL/INSTALLATION.
 
REPLACE LH 490 OVERHEAT SWITCH IAW AMM 36-11-08/401 490° F OVERTEMPERATURE SWITCH - REMOVAL/INSTALLATION AND
 
6. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.   
 
**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  
 
**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
